","notes":"Arrive after the posted opening time, view the current installation, and leave enough room to look across the adjoining plaza.","short_summary":"Make a compact, no-admission art stop on the undergraduate campus.","evidence_claim":"Lewis & Clark states that the Hoffman Gallery is free, open to the public, open daily from 11 a.m. to 4 p.m., and occupies 3,500 square feet.","source_url":"https://www.lclark.edu/hoffman_gallery/","source_title":"Ronna and Eric Hoffman Gallery of Contemporary Art","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"The gallery posts daily hours of 11 a.m.–4 p.m.; confirm the current exhibition calendar before visiting.","cost_status":"free","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"lc-first-weekend-college-outdoors","subject_type":"sequence_stop","entity_name":"College Outdoors","title":"Meet College Outdoors","subtitle":"Saturday midday · Map future weekend options","notes":"Find room 239 in Fowler, review the trip program online, and note where to ask about clinics or planning a later outing.","short_summary":"Locate the campus office that organizes recurring outdoor trips and clinics.","evidence_claim":"Lewis & Clark states that College Outdoors runs varied trips and clinics nearly every weekend during the semester and is located in Fowler Student Center room 239.","source_url":"https://www.lclark.edu/programs/college_outdoors/programs/","source_title":"Programs • College Outdoors","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Office access and participation require separate confirmation; trip registration, capacity, prerequisites, and fees may vary.","cost_status":"unknown","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"lc-first-weekend-pamplin","subject_type":"sequence_stop","entity_name":"Pamplin Sports Center","title":"Locate Pamplin Sports Center","subtitle":"Saturday afternoon · Learn the recreation hub","notes":"Walk to Pamplin, inspect the posted facility schedule, and note the nearby track and courts for future recreation plans.","short_summary":"Identify the main athletics building and its surrounding outdoor facilities.","evidence_claim":"Lewis & Clark identifies Pamplin Sports Center as the location of Physical Education and Athletics, while its campus map shows Pamplin near Fix Track and tennis courts.","source_url":"https://www.lclark.edu/sports/","source_title":"Sports • Lewis & Clark","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Recreational access and facility hours are not specified on the cited page; consult posted schedules and carry student identification.","cost_status":"unknown","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"lc-first-weekend-tryon-creek","subject_type":"sequence_stop","entity_name":"Tryon Creek State Natural Area","title":"Walk Tryon Creek’s Trillium Trail","subtitle":"Sunday morning · Explore the neighboring forest","notes":"Check conditions, choose the paved 0.3-mile Trillium Trail, and turn back before your route exceeds your time or comfort.","short_summary":"Try a short, defined introduction to the state natural area beside campus.","evidence_claim":"Oregon State Parks says Tryon Creek has eight miles of hiking trails and a 0.3-mile fully paved Trillium Trail with benches and turnaround areas.","source_url":"https://stateparks.oregon.gov/index.cfm?do=park.profile&parkId=103","source_title":"Tryon Creek State Natural Area • Oregon State Parks","source_kind":"government","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Open for day use year-round with seasonal closing times; trails may be muddy, and vehicles require a day-use parking permit.","cost_status":"unknown","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"lc-first-weekend-otterbus","subject_type":"sequence_stop","entity_name":"OtterBus","title":"Practice the Downtown Shuttle","subtitle":"Sunday afternoon · Learn the Portland connection","notes":"Check the live weekend timetable, board at the designated campus stop, and save the downtown stop before beginning the trip.","short_summary":"Finish the weekend by learning the college shuttle’s downtown connection.","evidence_claim":"Lewis & Clark publishes weekend and holiday OtterBus service information and identifies SW Broadway and Hall near Portland State University as its main downtown stop.","source_url":"https://www.lclark.edu/offices/transportation_and_parking/shuttle/","source_title":"OtterBus • Transportation and Parking","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Check the current weekend timetable and tracker before departure; weather or college closures can alter scheduled service.","cost_status":"free","under21_safe":true}],"warnings":[]}],"warnings":[]}
